1
00:06:20,000 --> 00:06:26,000
The extraordinary life story of Ray Charles.

2
00:12:40,000 --> 00:12:46,000
Ray is a drama, music film directed by Taylor Hackford.

3
00:19:00,000 --> 00:19:06,000
Born on a sharecropping plantation in Northern
Florida, Ray Charles went blind at seven.

4
00:25:20,000 --> 00:25:26,000
Inspired by a fiercely independent mom who insisted he make his own way,
He found his calling and his gift behind a piano keyboard.

5
00:31:40,000 --> 00:31:46,000
Touring across the Southern musical circuit, the soulful singer gained a reputation and then
exploded with worldwide fame when he pioneered coupling gospel and country together.

6
00:38:00,000 --> 00:38:06,000
Ray Charles, played by Jamie Foxx.

7
00:44:20,000 --> 00:44:26,000
Della Bea Robinson, played by Kerry Washington.

8
00:50:40,000 --> 00:50:46,000
Margie Hendricks, played by Regina King.

9
00:57:00,000 --> 00:57:06,000
Joe Adams, played by Harry Lennix.

10
01:03:20,000 --> 01:03:26,000
Jeff Brown, played by Clifton Powell.

11
01:09:40,000 --> 01:09:46,000
Fathead Newman, played by Bokeem Woodbine.

12
01:16:00,000 --> 01:16:06,000
Ray is a 2004 American biographical drama film focusing on 30
years in the life of soul musician Ray Charles.

13
01:22:20,000 --> 01:22:26,000
The independently produced film was co-produced and directed
by Taylor Hackford; it was written by James L.

14
01:28:40,000 --> 01:28:46,000
White from a story by Hackford and White.

15
01:35:00,000 --> 01:35:06,000
It stars Jamie Foxx as Charles, along with Kerry Washington, Clifton Powell, Harry Lennix,
Terrence Howard, Larenz Tate, Richard Schiff, and Regina King in supporting roles.

16
01:41:20,000 --> 01:41:26,000
Along with Hackford, the film was also produced by Stuart
Benjamin, Howard Baldwin, and Karen Baldwin.

17
01:47:40,000 --> 01:47:46,000
Ray was released on October 29, 2004, by Universal Pictures.

18
01:54:00,000 --> 01:54:06,000
It received generally positive reviews from critics, with particular praise for Foxx's performance and
became a box office success, grossing $124 million worldwide on a budget of $40 million.

19
02:00:20,000 --> 02:00:26,000
Ray received many accolades and nominations and was nominated in six categories at the 77th Academy
Awards, including Best Picture, and won two: Best Actor for Foxx and Best Sound Mixing.

20
02:06:40,000 --> 02:06:46,000
Foxx also won Best Actor at the Golden Globe, BAFTA, Screen Actors Guild, and Critics' Choice
becoming the second actor to win all five major lead actor awards for the same performance.

21
02:13:00,000 --> 02:13:06,000
Charles had planned to attend a screening of the completed film but died of
liver disease in June 2004, four months prior to the premiere.

22
02:19:20,000 --> 02:19:26,000
The film explores themes of blindness and impaired vision,
country music, jazz, loss of loved one, overdose.

23
02:25:40,000 --> 02:25:46,000
The tone is emotional.
